@startuml j4-staff-reply
!include style.iuml
title J4 Staff reply into the patient's chat
actor Staff
participant "Staff page\n(staff/index.html, staff.js)" as SP
participant "core.js" as Core
database "localStorage" as LS
participant "Chat page\n(index.html, chat.js)" as Chat
actor Patient
autonumber

Staff -> SP : opens /staff in the same browser as the chat
SP -> Core : FD.loadClinic(), then clinicEditor() and render()
SP -> Core : FD.tickets().sort(FD.byPriority)
Core -> LS : read frontdesk.tickets
note right of Core
Priority: urgent, needs human, answered, closed;
newest first within a status.
end note
SP -> SP : open ticket = the one chosen, else the first in the list
note right of SP
Only the open ticket's [data-ticket] holds #staff-reply
and #staff-send. "Needs human" older than 2 h shows
"over 2 h". Call list: needs human, or a booking not
closed, oldest first. Unknown list: "not sure" questions.
end note
opt Staff opens another ticket
  Staff -> SP : clicks its heading [data-open]
  SP -> SP : openId = that ticket, draft cleared, render()
end
Staff -> SP : types in #staff-reply, presses #staff-send (or Ctrl+Enter)
alt the box is empty
  SP --> Staff : "Type a reply first."
else text entered
  SP -> Core : FD.replyToTicket(openId, text)
  Core -> LS : add {text, at} to staffReplies, set status, write frontdesk.tickets
  note right of Core
  Status after a reply: urgent and needs human
  become answered; answered becomes closed;
  closed stays closed.
  end note
  SP -> SP : render()
  SP --> Staff : "Sent. The patient sees it in their chat."
  LS -> Chat : storage event, key frontdesk.tickets (another tab)
  Chat -> Chat : render() when no question is pending
  Chat --> Patient : .bot-msg marked "From the clinic team" (no Listen button)
end
opt Staff closes the ticket
  Staff -> SP : "Close ticket" [data-close] (shown unless closed)
  SP -> Core : FD.setStatus(id, "closed")
  Core -> LS : write frontdesk.tickets
end
note over SP, LS : a new patient question raises a storage event that redraws /staff; it also redraws every 30 s unless #staff-reply has focus
@enduml
